{"failure_id": "FAIL-0fc1c0f5", "timestamp": "2026-09-08T04:04:44Z", "category": "config", "severity": "high", "error_message": "semantic-scan.mjs crashed ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND on every non-npm consumer: static import of typescript runs before main(), so the documented skip (no TS/JS files -> exit 0) was unreachable, and any drift-scan template invoking it failed closed with an unrelated error", "root_cause": "Top-level static import of an optional dependency; the lazy-load contract (skip when no TS/JS files) was documented but never implemented", "affected_files": ["scripts/semantic-scan.mjs"], "fix_commit": "47041a7b59fe3543939137920dc1841edc43d6fc", "regression_pattern": "import ts from .typescript.", "prevention_rule": "optional-language-toolchain imports in gate scripts must be lazy (dynamic import inside main, after the file-existence check) so every consumer of the gate works without that toolchain installed", "status": "resolved", "updated_at": "2026-09-08T04:04:44Z", "file_glob": ["scripts/*.mjs"]}
{"failure_id": "FAIL-13e90ecb", "timestamp": "2026-09-08T04:18:59Z", "category": "regression", "severity": "medium", "error_message": "regression_check.py blocked every commit touching a file with an ACTIVE warning-severity failure-registry entry, while its own report printed 'WARNING - Known Bug History' — advisory wording gating like an error, and an in-flight bug report could not be committed", "root_cause": "The Known-Bug-History file-match advisory ignored entry severity when computing 'blocking'; only the pattern-readd scan and guardrails-scan.mjs honored a severity ladder", "affected_files": ["scripts/regression_check.py"], "fix_commit": "8ac7527e1a985f59f212925d5b656e6875c855e3", "regression_pattern": "", "prevention_rule": "blocking decisions in the gate family must route through one severity ladder (is_blocking / ADVISORY_SEVERITIES): low|medium|warning|info report, high|critical|error or missing severity gates — a report label and its exit code must never disagree", "status": "resolved", "updated_at": "2026-09-08T04:18:59Z"}
{"failure_id": "FAIL-0a01dedd", "timestamp": "2026-09-08T04:40:38Z", "category": "config", "severity": "medium", "error_message": "gate findings dead-end at the terminal: agents fix or annotate violations with no path from a scanner hit / registry entry to a durable openspec requirement the traceability gate can enforce", "root_cause": "the gate family covered detection (scanners), record (log_failure.py) and coverage (spec_traceability.py), but nothing generated requirement skeletons from findings, so specs had to be hand-written per bug", "affected_files": ["scripts/findings_to_spec.py"], "fix_commit": "fdc86bfca41ae3c837b58177ffbdc8b775ca9891", "regression_pattern": "", "prevention_rule": "every gate output consumed downstream must ship its scaffolder in-repo — findings_to_spec.py bridges registry+scanner output to openspec format, tested against spec_traceability's own regexes", "status": "resolved", "updated_at": "2026-09-08T04:40:38Z"}
{"failure_id": "FAIL-b81fa0ea", "timestamp": "2026-09-17T19:21:18Z", "category": "runtime", "severity": "high", "error_message": "CLI error paths produced exit 1 + raw traceback instead of the documented envelope: decide() tuple unpacked backwards in _fail(), unwritable out_dir re-crashed the envelope writer, non-string/NUL outputs bypassed the except-OSError guard (AttributeError/ValueError are not OSError subclasses)", "root_cause": "exit code is a wire contract, but error paths were only tested on the happy shape; malformed-input classes (wrong type, NUL, unwritable dir, missing field) crash before/around the handler because Python exception taxonomy is narrower than reality", "affected_files": ["hub/coherence/__main__.py", "hub/coherence/evidence.py"], "fix_commit": "dbbb659d5a1955d5b7cd6c663107efc47ce975f0", "regression_pattern": "AttributeError.*has no attribute 'strip'|ValueError.*null character|raw traceback on CLI error path", "prevention_rule": "every exit-code contract needs a test that drives the REAL CLI with adversarial inputs per error class (non-string, NUL, unwritable, missing, malformed JSON) and asserts exit code + parseable envelope + no 'Traceback' in stderr — direct function calls cannot see that no caller receives the code", "status": "resolved", "updated_at": "2026-09-17T19:21:18Z", "file_glob": ["hub/coherence/*.py"]}
{"failure_id": "FAIL-f6228dda", "timestamp": "2026-09-17T19:21:18Z", "category": "config", "severity": "medium", "error_message": "regression_check reported '0 over hard limit' while the file-size rule evaluated no test file at all: tests/ absent from SOURCE_DIRS and the test_*.py matcher is a glob used as a literal in str.endswith(), so every test file silently got source limits or was never scanned", "root_cause": "gate scope drifted from intent: SOURCE_DIRS candidates added hub/scripts/openspec but not tests, and the endswith() matcher never matched a real filename — vacuously green", "affected_files": ["scripts/regression_check.py", "scripts/regression_sizes.py"], "fix_commit": "7e559ba5dc51a4e58726161900a592ac72dbfabd", "regression_pattern": "test_\\*\\.py|SOURCE_DIRS.*tests", "prevention_rule": "before trusting a size/scope gate, enumerate what it actually evaluates (call its own API with a known-oversize fixture); a gate that scans nothing must say NOT_RUN — scope lists and matchers need a self-test that feeds them a file they MUST flag", "status": "resolved", "updated_at": "2026-09-18T21:47:10Z", "file_glob": ["scripts/regression_check.py"]}
{"failure_id": "FAIL-6e7b6f84", "timestamp": "2026-09-22T18:52:43Z", "category": "runtime", "severity": "high", "error_message": "runner heartbeat unit exited 22 on every tick (hub rejected malformed JSON) while enrollment reported success", "root_cause": "ExecStart was an inline bash -c body emitted through an unquoted heredoc; systemd expands $ in ExecStart against the unit's environment, so the variables the body defined itself (DISK_OK, PODMAN_OK) arrived empty, the JSON went out malformed, and the hub rejected it. The variables that lived in EnvironmentFile (RUNNER_NAME, HEARTBEAT_TOKEN) survived, which is why the failure was partial and easy to misdiagnose.", "affected_files": ["scripts/runner-enroll.sh"], "fix_commit": "bfb7e9992906fbb35964cb9d4345116d62ac2bdb", "regression_pattern": "ExecStart=.*bash\\s+-c", "prevention_rule": "ExecStart must be a bare script path, never an inline bash -c body; runner-heartbeat.sh is installed and invoked instead, asserted by tests/test_runner_enroll.py", "status": "resolved", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T13:53:52.964513+00:00", "file_glob": ["*.sh"]}
{"failure_id": "FAIL-ac75444c", "timestamp": "2026-09-22T18:52:43Z", "category": "config", "severity": "high", "error_message": "second runner enrolled on one host overwrites the first runner's heartbeat token", "root_cause": "unit and env paths were hard-coded (devgate-heartbeat.*, ~/.devgate-heartbeat.env), so every enroll rewrote one shared env file and all timers read it - the wrong runner reported under the other's name", "affected_files": ["scripts/runner-enroll.sh"], "fix_commit": "bfb7e9992906fbb35964cb9d4345116d62ac2bdb", "regression_pattern": "TICKET_FILE=\"\\$HOME/\\.devgate-heartbeat\\.env\"", "prevention_rule": "every unit and env path derives from the runner name via set_unit_paths(); asserted by test_second_enroll_does_not_clobber_the_first", "status": "resolved", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T13:53:52.964513+00:00", "file_glob": ["*.sh"]}
{"failure_id": "FAIL-8f9249ca", "timestamp": "2026-09-25T01:42:34Z", "category": "config", "severity": "medium", "error_message": "the file-size gate sized sixteen languages and not the one this repository's fleet-side scripts are written in: SOURCE_EXTENSIONS listed .ts through .cs and no .sh, so scripts/ was walked and every shell script in it was skipped. scripts/runner-enroll.sh reached 589 lines against a 500-line limit with the FILE-SIZE CHECK reporting nothing. Filed WITHOUT regression_pattern for the reason recorded on FAIL-20cc1a39: the defect is an ABSENCE from a scope list, so no line regex expresses it — every faithful pattern would have to match the SOURCE_EXTENSIONS literal, which the fix commit itself edits, false-firing on the very change that closes it. The guard is the scope self-test and the mutation battery, not a regex", "root_cause": "gate scope drifted from intent again, one declaration over from FAIL-f6228dda: that package fixed the MATCHER half (a glob used as a literal in endswith()), this one is the SCOPE half (the extension list). A hand-maintained scope list has no way to report what it is not looking at, so the gate returns '0 over hard limit' for a language it never parsed, and that is indistinguishable from a clean tree", "affected_files": ["scripts/regression_sizes.py"], "fix_commit": "92162de33d960e9d541b2bf405044341a572e8b7", "regression_pattern": "", "prevention_rule": "enumerate what a size/scope gate actually evaluates before trusting it, and test the scope DECLARATION itself: every extension and directory the gate claims to cover needs a fixture it MUST flag. The mutation battery found the second half of this one — `scripts` in SOURCE_DIRS was asserted by nothing, so the new .sh entry rested on a declaration no test depended on. See tests/mutation_battery_size_scope.py (3/3 killed, 1/1 control behaved)", "status": "resolved", "updated_at": "2026-09-25T01:42:34Z"}
{"failure_id": "FAIL-9f59c959", "timestamp": "2026-09-27T18:14:09Z", "category": "config", "severity": "high", "error_message": ".html was absent from SOURCE_EXTENSIONS in both scanners, so a single-file HTML game -- the entire artifact, one file -- was never pattern-scanned and never size-checked while both gates reported clean", "root_cause": "The scope list named fifteen languages and omitted the one this project was actually written in. The pattern scanner walks the project root, so the file was in its walk the whole time; only the extension filter kept it out. A clean report therefore carried no information -- the gate-vacuous-01 shape, arriving through the extension list rather than a directory.", "affected_files": ["scripts/guardrails-scan.mjs", "scripts/regression_sizes.py"], "fix_commit": "c246fd5", "regression_pattern": "^\\s+\\\"\\.sh\\\", \\\"\\.zig\\\"\\s*\\)", "prevention_rule": "Adding an extension is not enough on its own: assert a MUST-flag fixture in that extension AND an under-limit one that stays silent, and check whether the scanner's comment-syntax list already covers it (the .zig fix shipped without its language semantics and made doc comments fire as code).\n\nPattern tightened 2026-09-29 from `\\.html`, which matched the FIX (SOURCE_EXTENSIONS gained .html) and not the defect (its absence). The narrowed form is the pre-fix continuation-line shape ending at '.zig', so a real reintroduction of the missing-extension list still fires while the legitimate TEST_PREFIX_EXTENSIONS tuple does not. Absence-class defects keep their real guard in the prevention rule (must-flag fixtures in that extension) — see FAIL-8f9249ca.", "status": "resolved", "updated_at": "2026-09-29T00:00:00Z", "file_glob": ["scripts/regression_sizes.py"]}
{"failure_id": "FAIL-3619d624", "timestamp": "2026-09-27T18:14:09Z", "category": "config", "severity": "medium", "error_message": "The file-size gate never walks the repo ROOT: SOURCE_DIRS is built from a fixed candidate list (src, lib, app, scripts, tests, ...) that does not include it, so a single-file artifact at <root>/index.html is unsized even with .html in SOURCE_EXTENSIONS", "root_cause": "Source directories are discovered by name from a fixed candidate list, which assumes source lives in a conventional subdirectory. A single-file game or a root-level entry point falls outside every candidate while the gate still reports '0 over hard limit'. Found the same day as the .html gap and only visible because that one was fixed first: adding the extension looked like it closed the hole, and did not. MEASURED 2026-09-27 with the gate's own check_file_sizes across every DevGate-active repo: including the root would newly flag 5 repos -- DevGate 2 (unchanged), zombie-hero-match 2, zombie X pinball 1, ctrl-alt-defeat 1, radredeye 10, and Zombie Diver 35. The bulk are vendored and cache trees the scope contract does not yet name: external/, zig-pkg/ and .zig-cache/. So the change is a scope-contract widening plus a multi-repo cleanup, which is why it is deferred rather than half-done.", "affected_files": ["scripts/regression_check.py"], "fix_commit": "pending", "regression_pattern": "SOURCE_DIRS = \\[\\]", "prevention_rule": "To close this: (1) extend .guardrails/scope.json skip_dirs with the vendored/cache trees the repos actually use (external, zig-pkg, .zig-cache), (2) add the repo root to the SOURCE_DIRS candidates, (3) re-run the per-repo measurement and bring each oversize artifact under the hard limit or declare it in that project's overlay. A project whose artifact sits at the root can already keep its sources in a sized directory instead -- which is what zombie-hero-match did by splitting into src/.", "status": "active", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T18:14:09Z", "file_glob": ["scripts/regression_check.py"]}
{"failure_id": "FAIL-8a90d193", "timestamp": "2026-09-27T18:14:10Z", "category": "test", "severity": "medium", "error_message": "Editing a constant that a mutation battery anchors on silently disables the mutation, which the battery correctly reports as a build failure ('anchor appears 0 times, not 1')", "root_cause": "The battery mutates exact literal strings in the source under test. A one-character change to that literal means the mutation no longer applies, and a mutation that does not apply reports 'survived' -- indistinguishable from a guard that cannot be killed. The battery treats a stale anchor as its own failure for exactly this reason.", "affected_files": ["tests/mutation_battery_size_scope.py"], "fix_commit": "2312ceb", "regression_pattern": "", "prevention_rule": "When changing a literal that a battery anchors on, re-point the anchor constants in the same commit. The batteries need fcntl and cannot run on Windows -- reproduce the anchor assertion directly (each FROM anchor appears exactly once in its own target, each TO anchor zero times) rather than skipping the check.", "status": "resolved", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T18:14:10Z"}
{"failure_id": "FAIL-2026091901", "timestamp": "2026-09-19T14:30:00Z", "category": "config", "severity": "critical", "error_message": "Pinned evaluator image cannot process any request: runtime resolved frozen schemas through openspec/changes/devgate-spec-coherence-service/schemas, which the Containerfile (COPY hub/ only) never ships — every in-container invocation died exit 30 with 'malformed request: No such file or directory: /app/openspec/...', and the only real-container test asserted that same exit code for an invalid request, so it passed while the service was broken", "root_cause": "runtime contracts resolved through repository/change-package layout instead of the service package; the smoke test asserted an exit code achievable by a broken service (no valid-request case)", "affected_files": ["hub/coherence/__main__.py", "hub/coherence/schemacheck.py", "container/Containerfile", "tests/test_hub_coherence_container.py"], "fix_commit": "2fbaee2", "regression_pattern": "devgate-spec-coherence-service/schemas", "prevention_rule": "coh-rt-08: frozen runtime schemas resolve relative to the service package and ship inside the image (never through change-package layout); coh-rt-09: container smoke evidence must include a valid-request non-ERROR case and rejection reasons must name the invalid input, not an I/O error", "status": "resolved", "file_glob": ["hub/coherence/*.py"], "updated_at": "2026-09-19T04:55:07Z"}
{"failure_id": "FAIL-2026091902", "timestamp": "2026-09-19T04:53:58Z", "category": "regression", "severity": "critical", "error_message": "semantic-scan.mjs and run-tests.mjs escaped to the PARENT of a standalone DevGate clone: findProjectRoot walked up and returned its start dir when no marker was found, so semantic-scan crashed on a sibling's EACCES or scanned stranger trees, and run-tests reported '0 passed, 0 failed across 0 files' exit 0 while the repo's own tests sat unrun", "root_cause": "the guardrails-scan.mjs .devgate-basename layout contract was never ported to the other two scanners; three divergent root detectors", "affected_files": ["scripts/semantic-scan.mjs", "scripts/run-tests.mjs"], "fix_commit": "8a797b2", "regression_pattern": "findProjectRoot\\(resolve\\(devgateRoot, \"\\.\\.\"\\)\\)|walk's start", "prevention_rule": "every scanner resolves the project root by layout contract (submodule: parent of .devgate; standalone: the repo itself) or DEVGATE_PROJECT_ROOT; tests/test_scanner_root_anchor.mjs runs all scanners in a markerless parent fixture and asserts they never observe siblings", "status": "resolved", "file_glob": ["scripts/*.mjs"], "updated_at": "2026-09-19T04:55:07Z"}
